Lance Vesper is a tall, lanky human who looks far older than he is: pale, with deep bags under rheumy eyes, and an air of long illness. He wears a [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] uniform four sizes too large for him, taken from someone far bulkier, and several belts hung with utility pouches.

He is in his mid-twenties, alive and human, and denies being a lich. What ails him is a curse laid on him by a coven of nighthags, whom he angered in a swamp years ago, when he was younger and more arrogant. They drain his life to feed their own, so that he holds a quarter of the span he should have and looks it. He has perhaps five or six years left if the curse is not lifted, and no doctor can lift it. He is an overseer of the Scale, one of the troop under [[Org/The Scale/People/Ralph Bishop|Bishop]], and he hears the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]].

He is one of [[Org/The Scale/People/Ralph Bishop|Bishop]]'s troop, and stood with him against the [[Bestiary/Void|void-thing]] that came through the tear over the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor.
